s ice","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-7.choice2","label":"the fridge’s tray","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"the fridge’s tray","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-7.choice3","label":"a sealed box","rationale":"KEY","audio":{"text":"a sealed box","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}}],"answer":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-7.choice3","passage":"The class packed snacks for the field trip. Apples and cheese stayed in the fridge until morning. Crackers stayed in a sealed box on the counter. Ms. Reed checked both places before loading the cooler. She packed the apples and cheese last. The cooler already held ice packs beneath an empty tray. The crackers did not need to stay cold before departure. Their sealed box kept them dry instead. All snacks would travel together despite being stored separately overnight.","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":false,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[{"kind":"audio","role":"passage","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-class-packed-snacks-for-the-field-trip-apples-and-cheese-stayed-in-the-d00580d5f0.mp3","text":"The class packed snacks for the field trip. Apples and cheese stayed in the fridge until morning. Crackers stayed in a sealed box on the counter. Ms. Reed checked both places before loading the cooler. She packed the apples and cheese last. The cooler already held ice packs beneath an empty tray. The crackers did not need to stay cold before departure. Their sealed box kept them dry instead. All snacks would travel together despite being stored separately overnight."}],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-7","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"A new literal-detail question, with an explicit key in the exact recor