 Adults kept the jars away from children and loose coats. People brought bowls to the truck rather than cooking at home. The music made the wait for repairs feel shorter for everyone.","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":false,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[{"kind":"audio","role":"passage","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-power-went-off-along-the-street-neighbors-put-candles-in-glass-jars-on-4449e5de14.mp3","text":"The power went off along the street. Neighbors put candles in glass jars on their steps. Mr. Okoye brought his guitar outside and played songs. The food truck could cook using its own gas. It kept serving warm meals while people listened. The streetlamps were dark, but the small flames marked each doorstep. Adults kept the jars away from children and loose coats. People brought bowls to the truck rather than cooking at home. The music made the wait for repairs feel shorter for everyone."}],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-22","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"A new literal-detail question, with an explicit key in the exact recorded source passage. Public passage familiarity is unknown; known source-family exposure excludes it."}},"audio":{"instruction":{"text":"What instrument did Mr. Okoye play?","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},"passage":{"text":"The power went off along the street. Neighbors put candles in glass jars on their steps. Mr. Okoye brought his guitar outside and played songs. The food truck could cook using its own gas. It kept serving warm meals while people listened. The streetlamps were dark, but the small flames marked each doorstep. Adults kept the jars away from children and loose coats. People brought bowls to the truck rather than cooking at home. The music made the wait for repairs feel shorter for everyone.","path":"/au