","rationale":"KEY","audio":{"text":"heavy wind","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-29.choice3","label":"thick fog","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"thick fog","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}}],"answer":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-29.choice2","passage":"The morning ferry left at nine and took thirty minutes. Its afternoon return left at three and took forty minutes. Heavy wind slowed the return journey. The ticket listed a departure time for each trip separately. The outward crossing ended at the island before the shops opened. On the way home, waves pushed against the ferry's bow. The crew still followed the usual route past the lighthouse. The longer trip took ten extra minutes, rather than several hours.","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":false,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[{"kind":"audio","role":"passage","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-morning-ferry-left-at-nine-and-took-thirty-minutes-its-afternoon-retur-ca7e3310cb.mp3","text":"The morning ferry left at nine and took thirty minutes. Its afternoon return left at three and took forty minutes. Heavy wind slowed the return journey. The ticket listed a departure time for each trip separately. The outward crossing ended at the island before the shops opened. On the way home, waves pushed against the ferry's bow. The crew still followed the usual route past the lighthouse. The longer trip took ten extra minutes, rather than several hours."}],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.listening_stories.t2.2-29","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"A new literal-detail question, with an explicit key in the exact recorded source passage. Public passage familiarity is unknown; known source-family exposure excludes it."}},"audio":{"instruction":{"text":"What slowed the return j