eaf found?","choices":[{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice1","label":"rock from a quarry","rationale":"KEY","audio":{"text":"rock from a quarry","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice2","label":"the museum garden","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"the museum garden","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice3","label":"soil from a riverbank","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"soil from a riverbank","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}}],"answer":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice1","passage":"The museum displayed a fossil leaf beside a modern leaf. The fossil lay flat inside a locked case. The modern leaf sat in a small clear pot on the same shelf. A label explained that the fossil had been found in rock from an old quarry. The modern leaf came from a tree in the museum garden. Visitors could use a nearby magnifying glass to compare the patterns, but they could not open the case or touch either leaf.","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":true,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"The stated detail answers \"Where was the fossil leaf found?\". The alternatives contradict that detail or name another stated object. Passage replay is forbidden."}},"audio":{"instruction":{"text":"Where was the fossil leaf found?","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},"choices":[{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice1","text":"rock from a quarry","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice2","text":"the museum garden","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-30.choice3","te