nd direction. A thermometer recorded the air temperature. Each morning, three children checked one tool each. On Thursday, the bottle held water up to the second mark. The paper arrow pointed toward the school gate, and the thermometer showed twelve degrees. Their notebook had a separate column for every measurement, with the date at the start of the row.","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":true,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-31","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"The stated detail answers \"Which tool showed wind direction?\". The alternatives contradict that detail or name another stated object. Passage replay is forbidden."}},"audio":{"instruction":{"text":"Which tool showed wind direction?","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},"choices":[{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-31.choice1","text":"the plastic bottle","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-31.choice2","text":"the thermometer","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-31.choice3","text":"the paper arrow","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}]},"exposure":{"itemStatus":"reserved_original_question","priorExposureStatus":"unknown","sourceReuse":"none","limitation":"New reserved text; learner exposure must still be checked at family level."},"editorial":{"note":"The stated detail answers \"Which tool showed wind direction?\". The alternatives contradict that detail or name another stated object. Passage replay is forbidden.","keyReview":"one-explicit-key","originality":"original_reserved_content"},"retentionOnly":false,"nonGating":false},{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32","instrument":"adaptive_progress","reservedPurpose":"progress_test","contentStandardVersion":3,"trackId":"reading_stories","reportStrandId":"reading_stories","construct":"printed_literal_detail_retrieval","modality":"print","difficultyTier":2,"difficultyVersion":"progress-ordinal-2026-10-02.1","difficultyRationale":"Retrieve a precise explicit detail across several printed sentences with competing details.","stimulusFamilyId":"progress:reading_stories:6f2771ac111ec5ef08b5","enemyItemGroups":["progress:reading_stories:6f2771ac111ec5ef08b5"],"formatType":"PROGRESS_READING_DETAIL","prompt":"Which part received a patch?","choices":[{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice1","label":"the upper leather","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"the upper leather","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice2","label":"the sole","rationale":"KEY","audio":{"text":"the sole","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}},{"id":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice3","label":"the heel","rationale":"D-OPPOSITE","audio":{"text":"the heel","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}}],"answer":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice2","passage":"A shoemaker explained how she repaired a worn shoe. Its sole had a hole, but the upper leather was still strong. She cut a patch for the sole and glued it firmly into place. The heel needed no repair. After the glue dried, she checked the edges of the patch and trimmed a loose corner. She returned the shoe with its original laces. The owner tried it on and walked across the shop to test the repaired sole.","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"suppressStimulusAudio":true,"allowsChoiceAudio":true,"media":{"requiredSources":[],"decision":{"itemId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"not-applicable-no-pictures","rationale":"The stated detail answers \"Which part received a patch?\". The alternatives contradict that detail or name another stated object. Passage replay is forbidden."}},"audio":{"instruction":{"text":"Which part received a patch?","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},"choices":[{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice1","text":"the upper leather","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice2","text":"the sole","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"},{"choiceId":"lpp.reading_stories.t2.2-32.choice3","text":"the heel","path":"","required":false,"fallback":"speech_access"}]},"exposure":{"itemStatus":"reserved_original_question","priorExposureStatus":"unknown","sourceReuse":"none","limitation":"New reserved text; learner exposure must still be checked at family level."},"editorial":{"note":"The stated detail answers \"Which part received a patch?\". The alternatives contradict that detail or name another stated object. Passage replay is forbidden.","keyReview":"one-explicit-key","originality":"original_reserved_content"},"retentionOnly":false,"nonGating":false}]$progress_bank$::jsonb)
